# The second page: the greeting, and whether this computer can install at all (plan/23).
#
# GENERATED from config/calamares/modules/greeting.conf.in by stage 40.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE REPLACED, TWICE. It began as modules/welcome.conf.in, configuring the stock
# `welcome` module; plan/22 folded it into modules/language.conf when that module took the checks
# over; plan/23 split it out again, because the page that reports a verdict and the page that asks
# for a language are two steps in the sidebar and should be two modules. The numbers and the
# reasoning below have not changed through any of it — they were never about which module read
# them.
#
# The one thing that did change, and it is why the block exists at all: `requiredStorage: 32.0` was
# DISCARDED AT STARTUP for the whole life of the stock module. The ebuild builds Calamares with
# -DCMAKE_DISABLE_FIND_PACKAGE_LIBPARTED=ON, and GeneralRequirements.cpp:357 responds to
# -DWITHOUT_LIBPARTED by removing "storage" from both the check list and the required list with
# nothing but a cWarning. There was no disk row on the page and nothing blocked Next; a 16 GiB
# target reached the partition step before anything noticed. The module reading this file does the
# check itself, over /sys/block, excluding the disk the medium booted from.
---
requirements:
    # DECIMAL GB since plan/24 §3 — the unit printed on the disk, not GiB — and NOT A NUMBER
    # WRITTEN HERE. It is build.conf's MIN_INSTALL_DISK_GB, which modules/disk.conf renders into
    # `minimumDiskSize` as well, so the page that decides whether Next may be pressed and the page
    # that decides which disks are selectable are reading one value. They used to be two numbers
    # in two units, and the failure that pairing produces has no error message: an installer that
    # says this computer can install and then offers no disk to install onto.
    #
    # What the number has to cover is the layout, not a round figure: a 1 GiB ESP, two
    # @ROOT_SLOT_SIZE_MIB@ MiB root slots and enough /var for the seeded Flatpak store and a home
    # directory. The second root slot is not optional — it is the inactive half of the A/B pair
    # systemd-sysupdate writes into (plan/01), so a disk that cannot hold it produces a machine
    # that installs and then can never update. validate_config() in scripts/lib/common.sh does
    # that arithmetic rather than leaving it to this comment.
    #
    # ENFORCED, which it was not for the whole life of the stock module. The check measures the
    # largest block device that is NOT the one this medium booted from. Until plan/24 that
    # exclusion was also `PartUtils::getDevices( WritableOnly )`'s, applied by a stock module we
    # no longer run; the `disk` page implements its own and states the reason on screen, and the
    # two are now the same rule written twice on purpose — see plan/24 §6.
    requiredStorage:    @MIN_INSTALL_DISK_GB@
    # Plasma 6 Wayland. Under this the session runs but swaps.
    requiredRam:        4.0
    internetCheckUrl:   "@HOME_URL@"
    check:
        - storage
        - ram
        - power
        - internet
        - root
        - screen
    # REQUIRED is the short list, and internet is deliberately not on it. This installer writes a
    # payload that already travels on the stick — root image, UKI and the Flatpak store — so an
    # install with no network at all is a supported, first-class path (build.conf's
    # INSTALLER_PAYLOAD_FLATPAKS, and stage 90's whole reason for existing). The check still
    # RUNS, so the page shows the state; it just does not block.
    #
    # It is also why GreetingConfig's verdict has two states and not upstream's four: the box this
    # page borrows from the stock module says "can continue, but some features might be disabled"
    # for any unsatisfied recommendation, and nothing whatsoever is disabled by installing this
    # image offline. The rows below the verdict are what distinguish a blocker from a note.
    #
    # `power` is likewise informational: a laptop on battery can install fine, and refusing is
    # patronising. `storage` and `ram` block, because below them the result does not work.
    required:
        - storage
        - ram
        - root
